      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It creates a converter mapping code point 1 (`\\u0001`) to the encoded string `\"qor_5~yr2yEtVdG{\"`, then verifies decoding that string returns the original character. I'll improve it with meaningful names, a named constant for the opaque encoded value, and remove the deprecated `new Integer()` constructor.I made an error in the assertion — the expected value must remain `\"\\u0001\"`. Let me fix that.I'll rewrite the whole file with the correct assertion.The file has an invisible SOH character in the assertion instead of the `\"\\u0001\"` escape. Let me write it properly with the explicit Unicode escape:The original uses the `\\u0001` escape sequence but my file has a raw SOH byte. More importantly, I can make the expected value self-documenting by deriving it from the named constant. Let me rewrite cleanly:Now let me compile-check it:"
